// box_sedimentation_showcase_analytical_1000floaters_realgravity_density05_75k_collapsed_v3_lastbatch_floaterlog_gas.prm
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// UPDATE: back to a production/validation run now that the diagnostic phase below did its job --
// job 4131772 (this same config, logFloaterHistory ON, VTK off) confirmed restitutionCoefficient=0.5
// survives cleanly past step 35000 with zero LOW-RHO/DRY-LINK/NAN-LINK/MIGRATION-NAN/STALE-PARTICLE-IDX/
// AddExternalForces-NaN hits (vs. e=0.97's job 4131344 crashing at step 15000), so: timesteps raised to
// 100000, classic VTK output (fluid_field/particles/floaterBox) turned back ON at writeFrequency 2000,
// logFloaterHistory turned back OFF (verbose per-subcycle tracking no longer needed -- its own job is
// done), restitutionCoefficient stays at 0.5. The diagnostic-phase header below is kept for context on
// why 0.5 was chosen and what the collapsed-spawn/staggered-release setup is, but its VTK-disabled/
// logFloaterHistory-ON claims describe the PRIOR diagnostic run, not this one.
//
// UPDATE 2: that production run (job 4131856, 100k steps) still crashed, at step 33488 -- but NOT via
// the DEM-collision-cascade mechanism restitutionCoefficient=0.5 was chosen to fix: post-mortem found
// only 2/1003 floaters ever climbed meaningfully above spawn height (vs. 81/1000 at e=0.97), and the
// crashing floater itself had been resting quietly at the waterline for ~29000 steps with no recent
// DEM activity. The actual trigger was a [LOW-RHO] free-surface density corruption originating one
// block away (step 33482) and spreading via ghost-layer exchange into the floater's own block by step
// 33487 -- a fluid-side bug, independent of restitutionCoefficient, still unfixed. Lowering to 0.3 here
// is a further precaution against the residual DEM-cascade risk (the 2 remaining climbers), not a fix
// for the LOW-RHO crash, which restitutionCoefficient cannot address. Also: [DEM-WATCH] itself changed
// since job 4131856 -- it now triggers on penetration depth relative to body size (ParticleKernels.h,
// ComputeContacts) instead of a flat contact-force number, so it should surface any residual cascade
// activity more reliably at this new setting.
//
// logFloaterHistory sibling of the plain v3 prm below (job 4127217), whose statistical analysis
// (309 uids ever tripped [MEM-WATCH]/[DEM-WATCH]; 81 anomalous by Z>75, ALL from the 6 release
// batches at steps 4000-9000, ZERO from the first 4 batches at steps 0-3000) found that both
// diagnostics only ever caught a floater's launch AFTER it was already airborne -- max Z-range
// spanned within any single burst, across all ~1000 floaters and both magnitude-gated diagnostics,
// was 1.36 LU. Neither is threshold-gated tightly enough (nor exists densely enough in time) to
// show a climb actually happening. This prm uses ModelParameters.logFloaterHistoryReleaseStepFilter
// (new flag, ParticleKernels.h) to restrict logFloaterHistory's existing per-subcycle,
// magnitude-independent position+velocity(+force/torque/hydroForce/density) world-state snapshot to
// ONLY the 100 floaters released at step 9000 (the last batch -- heaviest single anomaly
// contributor, 17/81 by itself) instead of all 1000, which is what makes logFloaterHistory
// affordable here: the original all-floaters attempt (job 4124682) blew a 200GB quota at step
// ~18254 because that snapshot isn't dormancy-filtered and costs the same regardless of staggered
// release. Scoped to ~100 floaters instead of ~1000, full per-subcycle resolution for the entire run
// should cost on the order of ~1/10th that (order tens of GB, not hundreds) -- monitor `quota -s`
// regardless. Classic VTK output (fluid_field/particles/floaterBox, all keyed to the same
// writeFrequency) is disabled below (set to 1e10, same trick already used for domain_decomposition)
// since it isn't needed and the point is to save memory/quota for the CSV log instead.
//
// V3 of box_sedimentation_showcase_analytical_1000floaters_realgravity_density05_50k_collapsed_gas.prm
// (job 4124358, "v1"): that run collapsed every column's 10 stacked boxes onto one spawn plane at
// Z=64 (just 8 LU above the waterline at Z=56.024) with a 2000-step release interval, and crashed
// at step 6000 -- the render (steps 4k-6k) showed boxes already jammed into a tight overlapping row
// by 4k, then launching/tumbling chaotically, consistent with a DEM contact-overlap explosion
// (large interpenetration -> huge spring-force repulsion) rather than the LOW-RHO fluid-only
// mechanism characterized in the rest of this investigation. V2 (job 4124938, logFloaterHistory
// on) raised the spawn height to Z=118 (midpoint between domain top Z=180 and waterline Z=56.024),
// used a 1000-step release interval (10 batches of 100 floaters, all released by step 9000), and
// ran clean to step 15743 (zero [LOW-RHO]) before being cancelled -- not for a physics crash, but
// because classic VTK output alone (velocity+mapped_flag, ~3.7GB/dump at writeFrequency 1000) was
// on track to need ~466GB for the full 125000-step run, blowing the 200GB hard home quota well
// before completion. V3 keeps V2's spawn height/release interval (both already validated clean to
// step 15743) and drops "mapped_flag" from the VTK writers (velocity only) -- though that alone
// barely helps, since mapped_flag is only ~2% of a dump's size, the mesh geometry/connectivity
// (rewritten every dump regardless of which per-cell fields are kept) dominates. The change that
// actually matters is writeFrequency 1000 -> 2000 (~38 dumps instead of 75 over the shortened
// 75000-step run), landing around ~140GB total -- comfortably under the 200GB hard quota.
// logFloaterHistory stays OFF (see ModelParameters below) -- job 4124682's
// attempt with it on blew the 200GB hard quota at step ~18254, since the per-subcycle state log
// isn't dormancy-filtered and costs the same as a fully-active 1000-floater run regardless of
// staggered release.
//
// GENUINE 10x10x10 GRID (1000 floaters) sibling of
// box_sedimentation_showcase_analytical_125floaters_realgravity_gas.prm, same box size
// (halfExtents <3, 9, 3>), same real Y-neighbour-contact design (not the single-Y-position v6
// approach), same true g_SI=9.81 gravity. Domain scaled up proportionally in X and Y (160,160 ->
// 320,320) to give the same 32 LU column/row spacing for 10 positions each instead of 5; Z is
// UNCHANGED (180) since 10 rows at the same 11 LU spacing (64..163) still fit with 14 LU headroom
// to the ceiling. cellsPerBlock scaled proportionally too (40,40,20 -> 80,80,20), so the process
// count stays IDENTICAL at 144 (4x4x9) -- no new node/core budget needed versus the 125-floater run.
//
// SCALING: same avgParticleDiameterOverride/dxSIOverride as the 125-floater file (both decoupled
// from domain size by design -- see that file's own header for the full derivation) --
// avgParticleDiameter=8.001943372119138, dx_SI=0.000362694127490625, giving the identical
// liquidHeight=22.9016, floorHeight=33.1224, absoluteLiquidHeight=56.024 as every sibling in this
// family.
//
// GRAVITY: true g_SI=9.81 m/s^2, gravityOverride=2.1371500584054327e-05 -- IDENTICAL value to the
// 125-floater file (same dx_SI/dt_SI, since domain height Z and the override scaling didn't
// change). Eq. 10 (Buick & Greated 2000) incompressibility check: domainHeight(180) *
// gravityOverride = 0.00385, still far under the required <<1/3 -- stable.
//
// GEOMETRY: X = 16/48/80/112/144/176/208/240/272/304 (10 columns, spacing 32, same convention as
// the 125-floater file), Y = same 10 values (same spacing), Z = 64/75/86/97/108/119/130/141/152/163
// (10 rows, spacing 11, same clearance convention -- top row's box edge sits at Z=166, 14 LU below
// the domain ceiling at 180). 10x10x10 = 1000 boxes total.
//
// Densities: 5 distinct values, each assigned to TWO columns (columns 1&6, 2&7, 3&8, 4&9, 5&10) for
// statistical redundancy -- 0.5, 0.75, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0 -- rather than spreading into 10 distinct
// values; each density gets 2 columns x 10 Y-positions x 10 Z-rows = 200 floaters.
//
// Domain: <320, 320, 180> / cellsPerBlock <80, 80, 20> = 4x4x9 = 144 processes (2 nodes, multinode
// partition, IDENTICAL resource footprint to the 125-floater run).
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

BlockForestParameters
{
   cellsPerBlock                 < 80, 80, 20 >;
   periodicity                   < 1, 1, 0 >;   // X and Y periodic — no side walls, only Z floor/ceiling
   loadSnapshot                  false;
   storeSnapshot                 true;
   snapshotFrequency             10000;
   snapshotBaseFolder            snapshots;
}

DomainParameters
{
   domainSize         <320, 320, 180>;
   wavePeriods        1;
   liquidHeightFactor 2.862;
   floorHeightFactor  4.1393;
   initialAmplitude   0;
}

PIDParameters
{
   targetMeanVelocityMagnitude 0;       // still water — no flow forcing
   proportionalGain            2e-4;
   derivativeGain              1e-6;
   integralGain                2e-4;
   maxRamp                     1e-4;
   minActuatingVariable        0;
   maxActuatingVariable        1e-3;
}

PhysicsParameters
{
   enableWetting     false;
   timesteps         100000;
   Re                3100;
   Fr                1.31;
   We                15.6188;
   useHardcodedUnits true;               // keep fixed reference viscosity/relaxationRate; only gravity overridden below
   gravityOverride   2.1371500584054327e-05;  // true g_SI=9.81 m/s^2 -- see header derivation
}

ParticleParameters
{
   inFileName spheres_out.dat;
   bedCopiesInX 1;
   bedCopiesInY 1;
   densityRatio 2.55;
   fixingHeightFactor 1.5;
   frictionCoefficient 0.5;
   // Lowered from 0.97 (near-elastic -- 97% of impact velocity returned as rebound, independent of
   // collisionTime/stiffness for a linear spring-dashpot) to 0.5, a common moderate DEM default. 0.97
   // was never a Bogner-validated value -- his 2017 thesis (Sec. 5, p.109) explicitly states contact
   // forces were "insignificant" for his own scenarios and declines to even specify which collision
   // algorithm/parameters he used ("any method that prevents overlaps of particles could be used").
   // Diagnosed as the primary driver of the last-batch launch cascades (job 4131344): each collision
   // in a chain returned ~97% of the impact velocity, letting height/speed compound across 2-6
   // sibling hits per floater instead of bleeding off after the first. 0.5 was a first test of that
   // hypothesis, not a final calibration -- confirmed a dramatic improvement (2/1003 anomalous
   // climbers vs. 81/1000 at e=0.97, job 4131856), but not zero. Lowered further to 0.3 to squeeze the
   // residual cascade risk down further; NOT a fix for job 4131856's actual crash, which was an
   // unrelated [LOW-RHO] fluid free-surface bug (see this file's own UPDATE 2 header) that
   // restitutionCoefficient cannot touch.
   restitutionCoefficient 0.3;
   numSubCycles 10;
   useLubricationCorrection true;
   useNoSlipParticles false;
   useParticleBed false;
   avgParticleDiameterOverride 8.001943372119138;  // see header -- matches the family's own scale
   dxSIOverride                0.000362694127490625;
}

